 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: Papageno's \"Bist du mir nun ganz ergeben?\" and Papagena's \"Nun bin ich dir ganz ergeben\" (the libretto has \"gegeben\"), \"unsrer\" without an apostrophe, \"der Eltern Sorgen werden sein\" (the libretto has \"Segen\", blessing), with \"Sorge\" in the singular where the print has it (bars 110 and 112), the comma in Papagena's \"wenn viele, viele\" and none in Papageno's \"wenn viele viele\", and the repeats of the music (\"unsrer Liebe Kinder schenken\", \"Kinderlein\", \"so liebe kleine Kinderlein\", \"Papageno\" and \"Papagena\", \"Es ist das höchste der Gefühle\" and \"der Eltern Sorgen werden sein\"). The stammered names are written with as many \"pa\" syllables as are sung: where a run of them ends in \"-geno\" or \"-gena\" it is written as the name after its stammered start (\"Pa-pa-pa-pa-pa-Papagena\", sung Pa-pa-pa-pa-pa-pa-pa-ge-na), and a run that stops short of the name is written as the syllables alone (\"Pa-pa-pa\"). The stage directions (\"sie umtanzend\", \"ihn umtanzend\", \"ab\") are left out. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
